.TH HAMR 1 "2026-11-20" "hamr 0.4 preview" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
hamr \- turn EPUB, PDF, Markdown and plain-text documents into local audiobooks
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B hamr
.RI [ global-options ] " command " [ arguments ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B hamr
reads a document, renders narration using Breeze TTS2, checks the speech
locally, and assembles a chaptered M4B with a source companion.
An unresolved source or speech finding holds publication for review.
The packaged speech engine targets Linux x86-64 with AVX2.
Windows x64 CPU Q8 has passed checked publication and interruption
recovery. Windows Vulkan is a preview.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-home " DIRECTORY"
Use this app state directory. Place this option before the command.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Print versioned structured results. Supply explicit selections when
a command would otherwise prompt. Progress appears on standard error.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the installed version.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Show commands. Use
.BI "hamr " "command " \-\-help
for command-specific options.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B "setup"
Choose a recommended profile and download the speech engine and offline
speech checks. Use
.BI \-\-profile " PROFILE"
for explicit selection,
.B \-\-checks-only
to add speech checks, or
.B \-\-engine-only
to configure just speech generation.
.B \-\-ocr-only
sets up English scanned-PDF OCR with the installed Tesseract executable.
Use
.B \-\-ocr-profile auto
to add OCR during ordinary setup.
.TP
.B "doctor, profiles"
Describe this installation and hardware, or list speech profiles.
.TP
.B "voice cast, voice sample, voice select"
List the cast, preview an included introduction, or save a narrator
for new books. Use
.B "voice sample CHARACTER \-\-play"
to listen. Breeze uses the original reference recordings and transcripts.
.B "voice list, voice clone, voice design"
manage custom voices.
.TP
.BI "open " DOCUMENT
Review the plan, render, check and assemble a book.
Use
.BI \-\-voice " cast:CHARACTER"
to select a voice for this book,
.B \-\-yes
to confirm in advance, and
.B \-\-play
to play the finished book. Omit
.BI \-\-output " DIRECTORY"
to write under ~/Audiobooks.
.TP
.B "plan, profile, queue, worker"
Inspect a proposed reading, save reading preferences, create a queued
job, or process the queue.
.TP
.BI "resume " JOB
Continue a saved job using verified takes and speech observations.
.B "render"
also runs the full workflow by default. Use
.B \-\-max-new-takes
for a manual render batch.
.B "run"
exposes pipeline options.
.TP
.B "status, show, preview, excerpt, play"
Inspect jobs or source locations, audition a passage, export saved
takes, or play a ready book. For a publication hold,
.B "status JOB"
shows the planned output file and whether to resume the automatic
speech check or review a specific passage.
.TP
.B "repair, qa, review"
Apply a scoped correction, compare speech to the plan, or record and
resolve a listening finding.
.TP
.B "pause, cancel, cleanup"
Mark an idle job paused or cancelled, or inspect unreferenced data.
Cleanup previews changes unless
.B \-\-apply
is supplied. Published output is kept.
.TP
.BI "completion " SHELL
Print completion for Bash, Zsh or Fish.
.SH CONTEXT REVIEW
Ambiguous readings use the automatic policy by default.
Use
.BI \-\-context\-review " FILE"
to supply a local array of candidate replies, or
.BI \-\-context\-review\-endpoint " URL"
to request a review from a loopback HTTP service.
The service may request one follow-up with bounded source context.
Accepted choices are saved with the job.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Command completed. Use
.B "hamr status JOB"
to check the state of a saved job.
.TP
.B 2
Command or input error.
.TP
.B 3
Publication is held for an automatic speech check or a review finding.
.TP
.B 130
Interrupted. Committed work can be resumed.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B HAMR_HOME
Default app state directory. The legacy
.B AUDIOBOOK_HOME
also works. Explicit
.B \-\-home
takes priority.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/hamr
Default state, including models, snapshots and verified takes.
Existing owned legacy installations can use
.IR ~/.local/share/audiobook .
.TP
.I ~/Audiobooks/JOB-rREV/book.m4b
Default published audiobook path. The folder also contains
the source and companion files.
.SH EXAMPLES
Set up once. Accept the recommended profile at the prompt.
.PP
.nf
hamr setup
hamr voice sample nigel-thornberry \-\-play
hamr open "$HOME/Downloads/My book.epub" \e
  \-\-voice cast:nigel-thornberry
.fi
.PP
If interrupted, use the job ID printed by hamr.
.PP
.nf
hamr status
hamr resume JOB
hamr play JOB
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ffmpeg (1),
.BR ffprobe (1),
.BR mpv (1)
.PP
.UR https://github.com/MimirLab/hamr
Project and full usage guide
.UE
